# 1. Document Purpose

This Business Requirements Document defines the business needs, objectives, scope, business requirements, business rules and expected outcomes for the HR360 Human Resource Management & Analytics System.

The document establishes the business baseline from which functional requirements, technical requirements, user stories, process maps, APIs, database structures, testing scenarios and analytics requirements will be developed.

---

# 2. Executive Summary

HR360 is a centralized Human Resource Management and Analytics System intended to provide structured management of employee information and key HR processes.

The system will provide a common platform for:

* Employee management
* Department and role management
* Workforce status management
* Attendance
* Leave
* Performance
* Performance Improvement Plans
* Training
* Recruitment
* Analytics
* Management dashboards

The solution will combine transactional HR capabilities with an analytics layer to provide operational visibility and management reporting.

The system will use a PostgreSQL database as the central transactional data store, Node.js/Express.js REST APIs as the backend service layer and React/Vite as the frontend application layer. Microsoft Power BI is planned as the Business Intelligence layer.

---

# 3. Business Problem

The HR function requires consistent access to employee and workforce information across multiple business processes.

Without a centralized solution, the organization may experience:

* Duplicate data maintenance
* Inconsistent employee records
* Manual workforce status calculations
* Limited visibility of employee availability
* Fragmented attendance and leave records
* Difficulty tracking performance actions
* Limited visibility into employee training
* Manual recruitment pipeline monitoring
* Time-consuming reporting
* Inconsistent KPI calculations

HR360 is intended to provide a structured solution to these business challenges.

---

# 4. Business Objectives

| ID     | Objective                                             |
| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| BO-001 | Centralize employee information.                      |
| BO-002 | Standardize employee lifecycle management.            |
| BO-003 | Establish department-specific workforce status rules. |
| BO-004 | Improve attendance and leave visibility.              |
| BO-005 | Support structured performance management.            |
| BO-006 | Track Performance Improvement Plans.                  |
| BO-007 | Centralize employee training information.             |
| BO-008 | Provide recruitment pipeline visibility.              |
| BO-009 | Provide management-level HR analytics.                |
| BO-010 | Establish a reliable data foundation for Power BI.    |

---

# 5. Current-State Business Situation

The current-state model is assumed to rely on multiple operational records and manually coordinated HR activities.

Typical activities include:

```text
Employee Information
       ↓
Department / Role Records
       ↓
Attendance / Leave
       ↓
Performance / Training
       ↓
Recruitment
       ↓
Manual Reporting
```

This model creates opportunities for inconsistent data, duplicate maintenance and manual reporting effort.

The HR360 target state replaces fragmented processing with a centralized application and database.

---

# 6. Future-State Business Vision

The future-state HR360 operating model is:

```text
Business Users
      ↓
HR360 Frontend
      ↓
REST API Layer
      ↓
Business Rules
      ↓
PostgreSQL Database
      ↓
Analytics APIs
      ↓
Management Dashboards / Power BI
```

This provides a consistent flow from operational transactions to management information.

---

# 7. Project Scope

## 7.1 Employee Management

The solution shall provide centralized employee records containing information such as:

* Employee ID
* Employee code
* Name
* Email
* Phone
* Department
* Job role
* Work status
* Employment status
* Joining date
* Salary information
* Salary status

---

## 7.2 Department and Role Management

The system shall maintain controlled master data for:

* Departments
* Job roles
* Work statuses

Initial departments include:

* HR
* Operations
* Finance
* IT
* Sales
* Management

---

# 8. Employee Lifecycle Management

The system shall support employee lifecycle statuses including:

* CANDIDATE
* PROBATION
* EMPLOYED
* ON_LEAVE
* RESIGNED
* TERMINATED
* RETIRED

Lifecycle status changes shall be traceable through controlled API operations.

---

# 9. Department-Specific Active Status

HR360 shall not use one universal definition of an active employee.

Active status shall be derived according to the employee's department.

### HR

```text
employment_status = EMPLOYED
        ↓
ACTIVE
```

### Operations

```text
work_status = WORKING OR ONLINE
        ↓
ACTIVE
```

### Finance

```text
salary_status = PAID
        ↓
ACTIVE
```

Employees who do not satisfy the applicable department rule shall be classified as:

```text
NOT ACTIVE
```

The calculated value shall be treated as a derived business result rather than a manually maintained global active flag.

---

# 10. Attendance Management

HR360 shall support:

* Attendance date
* Employee
* Attendance status
* Check-in time
* Check-out time
* Working hours
* Remarks

Supported attendance statuses include:

* PRESENT
* ABSENT
* LATE
* HALF_DAY
* ON_LEAVE
* HOLIDAY

Attendance data shall support operational reporting and analytics.

---

# 11. Leave Management

The system shall provide:

* Leave type management
* Leave request creation
* Leave dates
* Leave duration
* Approval status
* Approver information
* Leave reporting

Initial leave types include:

* Annual Leave
* Sick Leave
* Casual Leave
* Emergency Leave

---

# 12. Performance Management

The system shall support:

* Employee performance reviews
* Review ratings
* Review feedback
* Review dates
* Performance history

The system shall also support Performance Improvement Plans.

PIP records shall include information such as:

* Employee
* Start date
* End date
* PIP status
* Review frequency
* Objectives / review information

---

# 13. Training Management

HR360 shall support:

* Training program management
* Employee enrollment
* Attendance status
* Completion
* Training scores
* Certificate status
* Employee feedback

Training participation shall be linked to employees and training programs.

---

# 14. Recruitment Management

HR360 shall support the recruitment lifecycle through:

```text
Candidate
   ↓
Application
   ↓
Screening
   ↓
Shortlisting
   ↓
Interview
   ↓
Offer
   ↓
Hire
```

Recruitment modules include:

* Candidates
* Job applications
* Interviews
* Job offers

Candidate and application statuses shall be controlled using approved status values.

---

# 15. Analytics Requirements

HR360 shall provide analytics for:

### Workforce

* Employee count
* Department distribution
* Active status
* Employment status

### Attendance

* Attendance status distribution
* Working hours
* Attendance trends

### Leave

* Leave requests
* Leave status
* Leave utilization

### Performance

* Average performance rating
* Employee performance distribution
* PIP monitoring

### Training

* Total training enrollments
* Completion count
* Enrollment count
* Average training score

### Recruitment

* Candidate pipeline
* Application status
* Interview activity
* Job offers
* Offer status

---

